  "scope": "Resident-device operations on NVIDIA L40/Warp1.19, setup/JIT/upload/readback excluded. Standalone cases have five repetitions per version measured serially. Refined-hand baseline is a fresh current-main run with three cached repeats; final has five. Torus baseline is the same main source from PR107 and both have three full solves. Initial integration suite failures and fix follow-up retained. The first full469 suite used default1024 clipping reserve; a final full suite tests the256-site automatic threshold and supported512 reserve in focused recovery tests. The lower test reserve bounds legacy clipping work. The first24 completion/seed memory tests passed before manually stopping the broad run during the first default-reserve hand test; that partial log reported0errors but does not certify the unfinished test. A separate complete7-case integrated memory run uses512 reserve. Runtime source is unchanged by these test-only settings. The initial automatic128-site threshold regressed torus-boundary128 and is retained in rawdata; final threshold256 repeats affected128/200-site cases. All other reported sizes select the same path. Native/memory tests explicitly enable facet recovery and are unaffected by the automatic threshold. Padded memory used8 graph phases; final lifetime uses4 first-replay phases, native audit uses4warm+4profiled phases. No CPU speedup claim; full hand mesher fails growth and remains tracked separately.",
